{"name":"Lime Lollipop","hex":"#b4bd7a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"lollipop","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An item of confectionery consisting of a piece of candy or sweet attached to a stick.","Something having the shape of a lollipop: a linear stem connected to a round body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prune the lower branches of a tree or other plant so that new growth appears only at the top, where more light is received."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lollipop"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lollipop","blocks":[{"text":"A lollipop is a type of sugar candy usually consisting of hard candy mounted on a stick and intended for sucking or licking. Different informal terms are used in different places, including lolly and sucker. Lollipops are available in many flavors and shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Farbenfrohe_Lollipops%2C_Austria.jpg/330px-Farbenfrohe_Lollipops%2C_Austria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lollipop","wikidata":"Q217446"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/500px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/1280px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG/500px-Rainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spiral type with multi-color","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARainbow-spiral_lollipop.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/500px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/1280px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg/500px-Tootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Tootsie Pop","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATootsie-Roll-Pop-Orange.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg/500px-The_Magdalen_Reading_-_Rogier_van_der_Weyden_%28cropped%2972.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3